From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:17:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] drm/msm/dpu: flush shared video CTLs once per kickoff
 (switch)

Bonded video interfaces on DPU 5 and newer share an active CTL, but the
kickoff loop triggers the same pending mask twice (needs_single_flush()
is false there, so master and slave each flush) and increments a slave
counter that the slave's vblank does not retire. The second trigger also
races the master's on the same CTL.

Submit the shared video CTL through its master only. Independent CTLs
and the command-mode and writeback paths are unchanged.

Based on the patch by slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com> in Project SunUEFI
(SM8750 port), patches/linux/7.3/
0023-dpu-shared-video-ctl.patch, without its vblank-timeout message
change. Here behind msm.dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush (default off) for an
A/B on the OnePlus Pad 4's bonded dual-DSI video panel.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 97fa68516346..c0a625b13211 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -411,6 +411,17 @@ module_param(dpu_vid_slave_late_cleanup, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpu_vid_slave_late_cleanup,
 		 "Clean a bonded video-mode slave up after the master's last frame (default: on)");
 
+/*
+ * A bonded video-mode pair shares one active CTL on DPU 5 and newer; its
+ * pending mask already holds both interfaces and only the master's vblank
+ * retires the kickoff. On: flush that CTL once, through the master; off:
+ * master and slave each trigger it, as upstream. Read at every kickoff.
+ */
+static bool dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush;
+module_param(dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush,
+		 "Flush the CTL shared by a bonded video-mode pair once per kickoff, through the master (default: off)");
+
 bool dpu_encoder_slave_late_cleanup(void)
 {
 	return READ_ONCE(dpu_vid_slave_late_cleanup);
@@ -3024,6 +3035,19 @@ static bool _dpu_encoder_kickoff_phys(struct dpu_encoder_virt *dpu_enc,
 
 		ctl = phys->hw_ctl;
 
+		/*
+		 * Bonded video interfaces can share one active CTL. Its pending
+		 * mask already includes both interfaces, and only the master
+		 * receives the vblank that completes this kickoff. Flushing the
+		 * slave again races the same CTL and leaves its count unretired.
+		 */
+		if (READ_ONCE(dpu_dual_dsi_single_flush) &&
+		    phys->intf_mode == INTF_MODE_VIDEO &&
+		    phys->split_role == ENC_ROLE_SLAVE &&
+		    dpu_enc->cur_master &&
+		    ctl == dpu_enc->cur_master->hw_ctl)
+			continue;
+
 		/*
 		 * This is cleared in frame_done worker, which isn't invoked
 		 * for async commits. So don't set this for async, since it'll
